& [JustificationIdentity] is the bounded lifecycle rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is b9b2481f-8cb0-4281-94a9-5ce9f04d07a3
  + [solution_uuid] is a52ae887-ae4f-4517-81eb-1202b211463c
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa

& [WhyNow] is a concrete runtime prerequisite
  + [cantord] already owns strict authenticated lifecycle operations
  + [cantor_mcp] already delegates Codex queries through the shared generation
  + [gap] is the process still requires manual launch and has no durable identity or health record
  + [future_value] is later manager design may depend on a proven lifecycle contract without acquiring it implicitly

& [WhyThisShape] is least authority
  + [operator_scripts] reuse the exact production server and client instead of duplicating service protocol semantics
  + [authenticated_readiness] proves the service rather than merely observing a PID or open process
  + [complete_identity] prevents stale PID reuse from authorizing shutdown
  + [atomic_state] prevents partial readiness records
  + [graceful_only] avoids broad process-control authority
  + [separate_logs] retain startup and runtime diagnostics without mixing machine output

& [Alternatives] records rejection
  + [PID_file_only] cannot distinguish PID reuse and is rejected
  + [port_probe_only] does not prove authentication, profile, or generation and is rejected
  + [automatic_restart] changes failure policy and is deferred
  + [Windows_service_install] changes machine state and administrative scope and is deferred
  + [manager_agent_now] lacks messaging, identity, authority, and effect specifications and is deferred
  + [force_kill_fallback] can terminate unrelated or semantically active work and is rejected

& [SecurityReview] is narrow
  + [token] remains reachable only through the existing service configuration and client
  + [state] explicitly excludes token path and token content
  + [process] is addressed by PID, executable, and exact start time together
  + [shutdown] is authenticated and generation-bound
  + [failure] preserves state evidence unless a just-created exact process requires cleanup
